# The build context travels through the Docker daemon's API on every build, so this file is what
# keeps a build from shipping the development machine inside it. node_modules alone is hundreds of
# megabytes, and the builder stage installs its own from the lockfile — the copied one would only
# be ignored later, after the cost of transferring it.

# Dependencies and build output: both are produced inside the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.turbo
**/.turbo

# Tool caches and reports that no build reads.
.fallow
**/.fallow
report.md
review.md
conventions

# Editors, agents and the repository itself. `.git` is not read by a build step: the image revision
# arrives as a build label, not from `git rev-parse`.
.git
.idea
.junie
.claude
.agents
.vscode
